    "userdoc.kctlref.intro": "<code>kctl</code> is the command-line interface for managing kcore clusters. Global flags: <code>-s</code> / <code>--controller</code> (controller address, repeatable for HA), <code>-k</code> / <code>--insecure</code> (skip TLS verification), <code>-c</code> / <code>--config</code> (path to config file), <code>--node</code> (node address for direct node commands).",
    "userdoc.kctlref.node.applydisko.cmd": "<code>apply-disk</code> <span style=\"color:var(--text-secondary);font-weight:400;font-size:.85em\">(alias <code>apply-disko</code>)</span>",
    "userdoc.kctlref.node.applydisko.desc": "Validate or apply a day-2 disk layout on a node, built on disko. <code>-f</code> names the layout file. Validates only unless you pass <code>--apply</code>; <code>--timeout-seconds</code> defaults to 300, and <code>--no-rebuild</code> skips the <code>nixos-rebuild</code> that otherwise follows an apply.",
    "userdoc.kctlref.node.applynix.cmd": "<code>apply-nix</code>",
